        "valueString": "Alert and orientated, mildly uncomfortable, not toxic; anxious and impatient."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neurological examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Cranial nerves II–XII grossly intact; visual fields full to confrontation; pupils equal and reactive to light; extraocular movements intact, no nystagmus. Face symmetrical; speech normal, with no dysarthria or aphasia. Motor power 5/5 in all limbs except left shoulder movement limited by pain and stiffness; no other focal weakness. Light-touch sensation intact. Finger–nose and heel–shin coordination intact. Gait normal; no ataxia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Head, ENT, and neck examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Scalp non-tender; no temporal artery tenderness or thickening; jaw opening painless. Ears and oropharynx noted as NAD. No meningism; full neck flexion painless."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
